Description: use a standard main() entry point
 The 4k version starts from a hand-written _start (with an x86-64 stack
 adjustment) and exits through raw x86-64 syscalls from sys.h, without the C
 runtime. This only works on amd64 and is not needed for the unpacked
 executable: use main(), gtk_init(&argc, &argv) and _exit(), and link
 normally against the C library and the GTK libraries given by pkg-config.
 This lets the demo be built for the other architectures (i386, armhf, arm64).
Author: Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>
Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
